spec: S06-12, S06-13, S06-11

`login` against the second server (profile `pw`: its owner @ana has the local password
`hunter2`; the profile carries the server and no token): the server prompt takes the profile's
server, `ANNOTARY_PASSWORD` answers the password prompt (echoed as `********`), the Token is
saved into the profile and works; a wrong password is exit 3; `logout` revokes the Token and
forgets it (the profile keeps its server); there is no default profile to offer (2026-10-21), so
`login` only notes `use it with -p NAME`. Merged stdout+stderr.

```console
$ ANNOTARY_PASSWORD=hunter2 annotary -p pw login
server [http://127.0.0.1:[..]]: http://127.0.0.1:[..]
password: ********
Signed in as @ana (owner). Saved profile "pw" → [..]/config.toml
use it with -p pw

$ annotary -p pw member list
@ana	Ana Lima	owner	*:read,comment,action,write

$ annotary -p pw token list --json name,status
[{"name":"first-run","status":"active"},{"name":"login","status":"active"}]

$ ANNOTARY_PASSWORD=wrong annotary -p pw login
? 3
server [http://127.0.0.1:[..]]: http://127.0.0.1:[..]
password: ********
error: wrong password — try again

$ annotary -p pw logout
Signed out (@ana): profile "pw" — token revoked and removed

$ annotary -p pw member list
? 3
error: profile 'pw' in [..]/config.toml has no token — add `token = "ant_…"` to it, or run `annotary login`

$ annotary -p pw token list --json name,status
? 3
{"error":"no_credential","message":"profile 'pw' in ~/.annotary/config.toml has no token","hint":"add `token = [..]` to it, or run `annotary login`"}

$ ANNOTARY_PASSWORD=hunter2 annotary -p pw login --json
server [http://127.0.0.1:[..]]: http://127.0.0.1:[..]
password: ********
{"profile":"pw","server":"http://127.0.0.1:[..]","handle":"ana","role":"owner"}

$ annotary -p pw token list --json name,status
[{"name":"first-run","status":"active"},{"name":"login","status":"active"}]

$ annotary -p pw token list --all --json name,status
[{"name":"first-run","status":"active"},{"name":"login","status":"revoked"},{"name":"login","status":"active"}]

$ annotary -p pw logout --json
{"profile":"pw","handle":"ana","revoked":true}

```
